// The registry itself, as data /api/dataset can serve without touching the filesystem.
//
// Everything between the markers is generated by scripts/build-site.py from
// data/entries.json. Do not edit it by hand: `python3 scripts/build.py` rewrites it,
// and CI rebuilds and fails on any difference.
//
// Why this is a second generated file rather than more of registry.js. That module is
// deliberately a validation table: entry ids, two grades each, titles, and nothing else,
// so an API check is an allowlist rather than a pattern. Widening it into a full copy of
// the registry would give it two jobs and make every proposal validation import 150 KB
// it does not read. Keeping them apart means each file is a function of one question.
//
// Why generate at all, rather than reading data/entries.json at request time: a Vercel
// function that opens a data file depends on that file being traced into the deployment
// bundle, which is a detail that fails quietly and only in production. The same argument
// registry.js and shell.js are already built on.
//
// ENTRIES is a *projection*, not the raw registry. /api/dataset promises a named set of
// fields; data/entries.json stays free to gain fields without breaking a consumer. The
// contract is documented under "The dataset endpoint" in docs/SCHEMA.md, and the field
// list lives in build_api_dataset() in scripts/build-site.py.

/*DATASET:START*/
